<title>PORTUGAL: Banco Espirito Santo boosts Q1 profit.</title>
<headline>Banco Espirito Santo boosts Q1 profit.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months ending March 31</p>
<p>(In billions of escudos unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		   6.92     vs    4.78</p>
<p>    Banking income		   34.78     vs   29.02</p>
<p>    Operating costs		  20.03     vs   17.91</p>
<p>    Net provisions		    6.52     vs    4.47</p>
<p>    Parent company net profit     5.11     vs    4.41</p>
<p>Note - Banco Espirito Santo is company name.  </p>
<p>Banco Internacional de</p>
<p>    Credito net profit		1.13     vs     0.25</p>
<p>    Banco Essi net profit	   0.39     vs     0.26 (loss)</p>
<p>    ESAF net profit		   0.27     vs     0.23</p>
<p>    Besleasing net profit	   0.22     vs     0.24</p>
<p>    Cons liquid assets	  3,449.00     vs 2,849.00</p>
<p>    Cons client loans	   1,579.00     vs 1,228.00</p>
<p>    Parent client loans	 1,117.00     vs   911.00</p>
<p>Unperforming loans as</p>
<p>    percentage of total	    3.5	 vs	4.6</p>
<p>Loans more than 90 days</p>
<p>    overdue			    3.1	 vs	4.1</p>
<p>Parent cover of unperforming</p>
<p>    loans (percent)		  122	 vs	104</p>
<p>    Cons cover (percent)	   112	 vs	 99</p>
<p>The positive trend over the first quarter was due to a combination of factors, including overall growth of activity and cost control.</p>
<p>Income from services and trading performed well but it would be &quot;prudent&quot; to expect slower growth over the remainder of the year, BES said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
